; screen_state.dta — active screen + render surface (global singletons).
;
; A `scalars` probe: runs fixed DTA programs and parses `key=value;` pairs.
; Deliberately split into two small program PAGES so each request stays under
; the console transport's ~1000-char script and 1023-byte reply caps
; (see tools/state_diff/budget.py).
;
; Run this FIRST when chasing a visual bug. If the two sides are not on the
; same screen, every other probe is comparing apples to oranges — the differ
; emits a `screen_mismatch` finding at the top severity tier because it
; invalidates the rest of the comparison.
;
; CAVEAT — UIManager::Handle short-circuits and returns 0 for most messages
; while InTransition() || InComponentSelect() (src/system/ui/UI.cpp:922-925).
; A zero here during a transition may be suppression rather than real state,
; so `ui.in_transition` is captured and the differ suppresses UI findings when
; either side reports 1.
;
; Requests: 2. Panel detail lives in the separate `panels` probe, which pages
; properly instead of inlining a whole nested walk into one reply.

(probe screen_state
    (doc "Active/transition/bottom screen, focus panel, transition state and render surface size.")
    (discriminates
        "the two sides are not on the same screen at all; mid-transition state divergence; render target resolution or aspect differences that rescale the whole frame")
    (kind scalars)
    (line_sep ";")
    (program_file "screen_state.ui.prog.dta" "screen_state.rnd.prog.dta"))
